    {
      "id": "dbxfe-m04-l01-card4",
      "revision": "1",
      "prompt": "Which step adds a rank to each inspection while keeping every row?",
      "answer": "A window function, evaluated per row over a partition and ordering; grouping instead collapses the rows to one per key.",
      "explanation": "RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY plant ORDER BY inspected DESC) gives A rank 1 and C rank 2 while both inspection rows remain, so the grain is unchanged. Check that output rows equal input rows and that ties and the frame follow a stated rule before trusting a running total.",
